  "question_stem": "A fair red spinner has 4 sides, numbered $1$, $2$, $3$, $4$. A fair blue spinner has 4 sides, numbered $0$, $1$, $2$, $3$. When a spinner is spun, the score is the number on the side on which it lands. The two spinners are spun at the same time.\n\nThe random variable $X$ denotes the higher of the two scores obtained. If the two scores are equal, then the value of $X$ is $0$.",
